  "source": "OpenLandMap Soil Texture Class, USDA system (ISRIC World Soil Information / OpenLandMap project), via Google Earth Engine -- a global statistical soil map, NOT an India-specific ground survey (Soil Health Card / ICAR-NBSS&LUP have no public bulk API as of 2026-10-21 -- see scripts/config.py's header above for what was checked and rejected).",
  "resolution": "250 m native pixel, surface (0cm) depth band",
  "band": "b0 (0cm depth) of SOL_TEXTURE-CLASS_USDA-TT_M/v02 -- the asset also carries b10/b30/b60/b100/b200 (deeper soil layers), not used here; this pipeline reports surface texture only, matching what a farmer standing in the field would judge by hand.",
  "method": "Per district/block/village polygon: ee.Reducer.mode() over the real raster pixels inside that polygon (the dominant texture class by pixel count -- a categorical class cannot be averaged, so mode, not mean, is the only honest reducer). Village/block tiers computed in ONE batched ee.Image.reduceRegions() call per district over that district's whole village FeatureCollection, not one GEE call per village.",
